{"type": "tool_call", "n": 5, "ts": 1790155602.9715772, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "UK ENTITY \u2014 TRAVEL (GL 6300), Q1 2026 \u2014 response to UK MD query\nPrepared by david.murguia@gmail.com, 2026-04-03. Source: UK ledger, functional currency GBP. Read-only analysis; no journal entries posted.\n\nTOTAL Q1 2026 TRAVEL SPEND: GBP 4,591.73\nTies to GL 6300 cumulative ending balance at 2026-03-31 (debit-minus-credit) of GBP 4,591.73.\n\nBY MONTH (period activity, GBP)\n- Jan 2026: 1,376.38\n- Feb 2026: 1,649.47\n- Mar 2026: 1,565.88 (March close still in progress \u2014 subject to late accruals/expense reports)\n\nBY MERCHANT (GBP / % of total)\n1. British Airways (airfare)   3,669.27  79.9%  \u2014 9 entries\n2. Premier Inn (hotel)           460.98  10.0%  \u2014 2 entries\n3. Addison Lee (taxi)            348.58   7.6%  \u2014 7 entries\n4. Trainline (rail)              112.90   2.5%  \u2014 1 entry\n   Total                       4,591.73 100.0%  \u2014 19 entries\n\nANSWER: British Airways is by far the largest merchant at GBP 3,669.27, ~80% of Q1 UK travel spend. Three London\u2013New York long-haul bookings alone account for GBP 1,940.40 (JE-00072 640.00; JE-00166 712.40; JE-00257 588.00), i.e. 42% of all Q1 travel.\n\nSUPPORTING ENTRIES (all UK, all posted to 6300 with offset to 1000 Cash, source = corporate card, all with support attached)\nBritish Airways: JE-00041 (01-08) 182.55; JE-00072 (01-21) 640.00 LON-NYC; JE-00083 (01-24) 149.80; JE-00142 (02-06) 145.52; JE-00151 (02-09) 453.38; JE-00166 (02-17) 712.40 LON-NYC; JE-00230 (03-02) 451.50; JE-00257 (03-10) 588.00 LON-NYC; JE-00275 (03-19) 346.12\nPremier Inn: JE-00074 (01-21) 238.65; JE-00145 (02-07) 222.33\nAddison Lee: JE-00042 (01-08) 65.82; JE-00046 (01-10) 24.60; JE-00097 (01-27) 74.96; JE-00127 (02-03) 70.13; JE-00172 (02-19) 45.71; JE-00258 (03-11) 32.48; JE-00285 (03-23) 34.88\nTrainline: JE-00246 (03-07) 112.90\n\nNOTES / CAVEATS\n- All 19 entries are debits; no credits, refunds or